  "body": "Found by a probe after PR #1663 (#1609). Upstream main 2b6e03f2.\n\n**What happens.** A 2D Contour with side Inside and `entry: Ramp` feeds straight down into the material at the cutting feed at each level. The path has no note. The cause is in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_bore.rs`, in the `Entry3D::Ramp =>` arm (near line 111). The chord goes from the leg to the ring start. On a closed ring, these are the same point, so the chord has no length. The code checks only the center cut (`contour_link::guard`). Then it pushes a `Feed` to `e2` at the cutting feed. This code does not use `descent::plan_arm`, so the fix of #1663 does not apply to it.\n\n**Repro.** `contour` on a square, half-width 20 at the origin. Tool diameter 6, side Inside, `lead: Lead::None`, top 0, bottom -6, stepdown 2, `entry: Ramp`, `blend_turns: false`, links `PLANAR`, retract 2, feed 500, plunge feed 250. The path has `Feed (-17,-17,0) -> (-17,-17,-2)` at 500 with no note. The levels -2 to -4 and -4 to -6 are the same.\n\nA Contour with side Outside is correct. It makes named axial plunges at the plunge feed.\n\n**Expected.** A ramp entry descends at no more than the ramp angle, for example as a zig-zag along the ring. If it cannot, it substitutes by name: a plunge at the plunge feed with an `entry:` note. A straight-down feed at the cutting feed with no note is never correct.\n\n**Done means:** a pin on the repro shows that every descending feed move is at most the ramp angle, or is a named plunge at the plunge feed. The pin is red on today's code and is mutation-checked.\n",
